<div xmlns:perseus="http://www.perseus.org/meta/perseus.rdfs#" xmlns:dctype="http://purl.org/dc/dcmitype/" xmlns:tufts="http://www.tufts.edu/" xmlns:alph="http://alpheios.net/namespaces/tei" class="alpheios-lex-text_container en">
    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n78084" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">παραιωρ-έω</span></b> , <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>A.</b><i>hang up beside</i>, 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">τινί τι</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Nonn.
					<u>D.</u>
					1.43
				</span></i>
			, etc.:—mostly in 
				Pass.
			, <i>to be hung</i> or <i>hang beside</i>, 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἐγχειρίδια παρὰ τὸν δεξιὸν μηρὸν
					παραιωρεύ μενα ἐκ τῆς ζώνης</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Hdt.
					7.61
				</span></i>
			, cf. <i><span class="en">
				Achae.
				19.2
			</span></i>; of persons, <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ξιφίδια παρῃώρηντο</span>
			<i>they had</i> daggers <i>hung at their side</i>, <i><span class="en">
				Hdn.
				2.13.10
			</span></i>: abs., of a suppliant, <i>hang upon another</i>, <i><span class="en">
				Plu.
				<u>Ant.</u>
				77
			</span></i>. </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense2"><b>II.</b>
			
				Pass.
			, <i>take passive exercise</i>, e.g. in a boat, <i><span class="en">
				Aët.
				9.30
			</span></i>.</div>
    </div> <div class="alpheios-lex-footnotes en"> </div>
